{
  "handle": "Decay",
  "mechanism": "Gradual attenuation: without reinforcement, {{value}} V decreases over time. `half_life` determines the rate. Reinforcement resets or boosts V. V descends to `floor_value` and stops there; reaching the floor triggers a {{state}} change, and removal only where the floor is zero.",
  "gloss": "Automatic expiration of stale state",
  "failure_modes": [
    "Unreachable removal: `floor_value` is above zero, so V never reaches zero and a removal trigger set at zero never fires."
